@startuml
title modify-business-process - edit an existing process
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor "AI agent" as AI
participant "MCP tool\nmodify-business-process" as Tool
participant "ModifyBusinessProcessService" as Svc
participant "ProcessDesignService\n(CrtProcessBuilder)" as PDS
participant "Terrasoft.Core" as Core

AI -> Tool : describe-business-process (MANDATORY before the edit)
Tool --> AI : current graph
AI -> AI : compose the operations array
AI -> Tool : process-name or process-uid + operations JSON
Tool -> Svc : ModifyProcess(env, request)
Svc -> Svc : exactly one identity (name XOR uid)
Svc -> PDS : POST { "request": { name, operations } }
PDS -> PDS : apply the operations in order\n(atomic: one failure rolls the whole batch back)
PDS -> PDS : re-apply auto-layout to the WHOLE diagram
PDS -> Core : SaveSchema
PDS --> Svc : { "ModifyProcessResult":\n{ success, schemaName, schemaUId, appliedOperations } }
Svc --> AI : schemaName + appliedOperations
AI -> Tool : describe-business-process (MANDATORY read-back)

note over PDS
  No structural validation on this path -
  only the create path validates the graph.
  removeElement cascades but does not
  re-join the flow across the gap.
end note
@enduml
